        "description": "Control real macOS apps. clipboard reads selected clipboard_formats (default text), or intentionally writes/clears the system clipboard without automatic restoration. Writes accept format=text/markdown/html/rtf/image/files; rtf_base64 and png_base64 supply binary formats, and file_paths must exist and be absolute. Image reads return bounded PNG previews as image content, with content_index in items; file reads return file URLs without opening files. Clipboard read/write does not paste into an app and needs no observation ticket. Reply/allocation safety boundaries: 64 items, 256 KiB text, 8 MiB encoded images and 64 MiB decoded rasters. list returns apps, visible windows and active displays. launch accepts exactly one bundle_id, absolute app_path (.app), or exact app_name; it defaults to background and returns the resolved process incarnation. arguments are literal argv for new processes; new_instance requests a distinct PID; open_urls delivers absolute URLs/documents to that exact app bundle. Running instances never silently ignore arguments, and ambiguous process reuse is rejected. Explicit delivery=foreground may activate the app. preview returns a read-only vision frame with preview_id and input_available=false, never creates or consumes an input ticket, and requires launch_time for window/app scope. Moving/resizing windows remain viewable; geometry_stable=false omits pointer overlays in the viewer. observe supports mode=ax (Accessibility only, no screenshot or Screen Recording needed), vision (screenshot only), or both (default; AX when available). scope=window (default) requires pid/window_id; scope=app requires pid and composes all its visible windows; scope=screen accepts display_id, defaulting to the main display. Screen scope captures the entire selected display, including other apps. AX elements include their owning pid/window_id; app menu roots carry anchor_window_id instead. Every input requires the latest snapshot_id and consumes it before delivery: observe again before another action. Coordinates are pixels of the returned image, across its full frame; AX-only observations accept elements and explicit screen/normalized coordinates, but no screenshot pixel coordinates. Choose an AX element, coordinates, or a text region_id, never more than one. recognize_text adds local OCR text_regions to screenshot observations and zoom, with confidence and top-left screenshot-pixel frames; region IDs expire with that snapshot. OCR reports visible text, not control semantics. press performs AXPress; click/scroll/drag use x/y. Background type/key/keys/paste require a confirmed target element. Background is default for window/app scope; screen input requires delivery=foreground (except AX press). Foreground uses the shared keyboard/mouse. type uses Unicode events in the background; another window uses writable AXValue computed from readable text/selection, with complete value and final-caret readback when supported. Background physical keys still require confirmed keyboard focus. Both routes confirm supplementary characters against readable text/selection; missing or transformed text raises text_unconfirmed without replay. Explicit foreground supplementary text uses one plain-text paste with clipboard preservation. text_route reports the chosen method. Use key/keys for physical shortcuts. key chords use CMD/CTRL/ALT/SHIFT, e.g. CMD+A or ENTER. dy/dx are signed scroll pixels. sequence executes explicit caller-fixed AX/keyboard steps, while the harness retains task planning and orchestration. hover reveals alternate AX UI or sends a targeted mouse move; moving outside or turn cleanup restores alternate UI. invoke_menu resolves exact path labels afresh after each native expansion, refuses ambiguity/disabled items, and never falls back to pixels. zoom captures a fresh native-resolution crop from screenshot-pixel x1/y1/x2/y2, returning a new vision snapshot whose pixel coordinates are relative to that crop; old 